Z||000000||Conrad Sanville||04-02-2000||08:18 AM||||<BR>Some boob backed into me and drove a <BR>trailer hitch through the door skin on <BR>the passenger side of my 85 SE.  What <BR>kind of a job is it to replace the door <BR>skin?  The door frame seems fine.||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||04-02-2000||09:04 AM||||It's not hard, just a little time consuming. You basically have to take the door aparts. Start with removing the inner door panel, because you have to get access to some hiddened fasteners. I'd probably just replace the whole door, it'd be easier maybe. I guess you would have to fart around with alignment if you did that. Six of one, half dozen of the other.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||04-02-2000||09:47 AM||||Check out Kick Hill Farms in Lebanon Ct. Phone # 860 642-4362/ fax 860 642-7107.  Bob Parker probably has the door panel in the correct color on site.  He may be able with the install or give recommendations on how to.  I'd never replace a door unless the door frame was bent in the accident.  I did that once.  They are heavy and difficult to manuver.  If you have power mirrors, windows, locks, lots of potential to screw up wireing.||||reg||3
Z||000003||Phil||04-02-2000||11:46 AM||||I've got an extra red one with gray molding in RI come and get it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||04-02-2000||01:14 PM||||I have a red passenger side door skin, too.  It would have to be shipped, though.  Let me know if Phils doesn't work out.  Email me for directions on how to remove the door skin.  Fairly easy if you take your time.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||04-02-2000||05:10 PM||||door skin notes are available by entering the Ogre cave via the link on the bottom of this page.||||reg||1
